<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Snow blankets part of Kansas.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Snow blankets part of Kansas.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Snow blanketed parts of Kansas and Oklahoma Thursday, providing a much-needed dose of moisture to the hard red winter wheat crop and causing some minor grain transportation delays, merchandisers said Friday.</p>
<p>The brunt of the storm hit Kansas' southern tier of counties, where five to eight inches of snowfall had been forecast.</p>
<p>&quot;It snowed all day (Thursday),&quot; said a merchandiser in south central Kansas. &quot;We received about six inches, and they got more in the southwest part of the state. In fact, it's slowing up rail traffic.&quot; But the dealer said the delays were not serious and would probably only last about half a day.</p>
<p>Cash basis bids were mostly unchanged, although one Gulf exporter lowered its bid by about two cents.  </p>
